Declare a character set on three tables.

nodegroup, federation and magnum_service are created without a character
set, while magnum's other ten tables and models.table_args() both ask for
UTF8. Declare it on all three, so the schema no longer depends on how the
server resolves a default that some tables state and others do not.

From MariaDB 11.5 a bare CHARACTER SET stopped resolving to the same
collation as the database default (MDEV-25829). nodegroup then lands on
utf8mb3_general_ci and cluster on utf8mb3_uca1400_ai_ci, and the join
between them in nodegroups_v2 aborts every new deployment.

Prompt: Michael asked what a Magnum-side fix for the MariaDB collation
failure would look like, given Magnum is the only service Kolla-Ansible
CI sees it in, and asked for it as a patch in a new magnum patch stream
so it can go upstream alongside the Kolla-Ansible changes.

